  "properties": {
    "title": "GRID3 NGA - Health Facilities v4.0",
    "description": "GRID3 NGA - Health Facilities v4.0 includes operational health facility points for all 36 states in Nigeria, as well as for the Federal Capital Territory (FCT). The dataset is a non-exhaustive, non-validated geographic representation of health facility points for all 36 states and the FCT. This release supersedes v3.0 (https://doi.org/10.7916/s6cq-1q98), which updated 23 states and the FCT, and supersedes GRID3 NGA Health Facilities v2.0 ( https://doi.org/10.7916/kv1n-0743 ), the last complete national release. The following changes were made: For all states and the FCT, the ward boundary attribute is updated based on the GRID3 NGA – Operational Wards v4.0 dataset. As a result, the flag5 attribute is updated, which indicates if health facility points fall outside the current operational ward boundary layer Major updates for the 13 states not included in v3.0: Akwa Ibom, Anambra, Benue, Cross River, Ebonyi, Edo, Ekiti, Imo, Lagos, Ondo, Plateau, Rivers and Taraba Minor updates for 11 states included in v3.0: Bauchi, Borno, Kaduna, Kano, Kogi, Kwara, Nasarawa, Niger, Ogun, Osun and Sokoto. Small numbers of health facilities were added or removed, mostly among records without xy coordinates No health facilities added or removed in the remainder of v3.0: Abia, Adamawa, Bayelsa, Delta, Enugu, Gombe, Jigawa, Katsina, Kebbi, Oyo, Yobe, Zamfara and the FCT. Keywords: Health Facilities",
    "license": "The data and accompanying document are licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International, CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0) and specified in legal code (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode)",
